{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/systems"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","symbolKind":"module","title":"Systems","modules":[{"name":"Systems"}],"externalID":"Systems"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A world holds data: entities and their components, and resources. A "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"system"}]},{"type":"text","text":" holds a rule: a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"step that reads part of the world and changes part of it, such as “every entity with a velocity"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"moves” or “gravity pulls on everything that isn’t frozen.” A "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"schedule"}]},{"type":"text","text":" lists the systems of one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"frame or step and runs them on a world, each once per run."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The examples throughout this module use these components, resources and event:"}]},{"code":["struct Position: Component { var x: Double, y: Double }","struct Velocity: Component { var dx: Double, dy: Double }","struct Health: Component { var current: Int }","struct Frozen: Component {}","","struct Score: Resource { var points: Int }","struct TimeStep: Resource { var seconds: Double }","struct Paused: Resource {}","","struct Damage: Event { var target: Entity, amount: Int }"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Declare a System","anchor":"Declare-a-System"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The simplest way to write a system is to mark a type with the ","type":"text"},{"code":"@System","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" macro and give it a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"run","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" method. The method’s parameters say what the system works on, and their types say how:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update","isActive":true},{"text":" writes components, a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Query","isActive":true},{"text":" reads them, and a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceReader","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reads a resource. The following two systems pull everything that isn’t frozen downward, then move","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it by its velocity:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["@System","struct Gravity {","    func run(_ falling: Update<Velocity>.Where<Without<Frozen>>) {","        falling { velocity, _ in velocity.dy -= 10 }","    }","}","","@System","struct Movement {","    func run(_ movers: Update<Position>.Over<Velocity>.Where<Without<Frozen>>) {","        movers { position, row in","            position.x += row.components.dx","            position.y += row.components.dy","        }","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because the parameters’ types state what each system reads and writes, the macro writes the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system’s "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for you: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Gravity"},{"type":"text","text":" writes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Velocity"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Movement"},{"type":"text","text":" writes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Position"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reads "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Velocity"},{"type":"text","text":". A schedule uses the access to decide which systems can run at the same time."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You can also conform a type to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" by hand and write its ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/run(in:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" method, which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"receives the whole world. See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for when to do that.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Run Systems in a Schedule","anchor":"Run-Systems-in-a-Schedule"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","type":"reference"},{"text":" is built from a list of systems, written in a result builder. Running it runs each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"system once. The following example drops a ball for one frame:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["var world = World()","let ball = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 100), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 0))","","let frame = Schedule {","    Gravity()","    Movement().after(Gravity.self)","}","frame.run(on: &world)","","print(world[Position.self, of: ball])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 1.0, y: 90.0)\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Systems run in the order you write them, unless an ordering constraint says otherwise.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"after(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"before(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" require one system to run after or before another; ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"names a group of systems so constraints can refer to all of them at once; and ","type":"text"},{"code":"runIf(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" skips","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a system when a condition doesn’t hold.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Systems whose accesses don’t conflict, because neither writes what the other reads or writes,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"run at the same time, and the world ends as though they had run one after another (commands","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"apply when each wave finishes). Systems that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"conflict run in order. When two conflicting systems aren’t ordered by any constraint, their order","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rests only on how they happen to be written; ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguities()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" finds those pairs so a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"test can keep a schedule free of them. To learn more, see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SchedulingSystems","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DeclaringSystems","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SchedulingSystems","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DrivingAWorldFromAnApp","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System"],"anchor":"Essentials","title":"Essentials"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemParameter","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceReader","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceWriter","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventReader","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventWriter","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/RemovedComponents"],"anchor":"System-Parameters","title":"System Parameters"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduleBuilder","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduledSystem","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Ambiguity"],"anchor":"Building-and-Running-Schedules","title":"Building and Running Schedules"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/MainActorSystem"],"anchor":"Main-Actor-Systems","title":"Main-Actor Systems"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/UpdateEvents","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ForwardEvents","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ForwardChanges"],"anchor":"Built-In-Systems","title":"Built-In Systems"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemProfile","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemTiming"],"anchor":"Profiling","title":"Profiling"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare the rules of a simulation as systems, and run them on a world in a schedule."}],"references":{"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemProfile":{"abstract":[{"text":"A resource that records how long each system takes to run.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"SystemProfile","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemProfile","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemprofile","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SystemProfile","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SystemProfile","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Ambiguity":{"kind":"symbol","title":"Ambiguity","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/ambiguity","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Ambiguity"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Ambiguity","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Two systems of a schedule whose accesses conflict but that no ordering constraint orders, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the order they run in rests only on the order they were written in."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Ambiguity"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemTiming":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The times one system of a schedule has taken to run."}],"title":"SystemTiming","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemtiming","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemTiming","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SystemTiming","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SystemTiming","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Update":{"abstract":[{"text":"A system parameter that changes a component of every entity that holds it.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"Update","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/update","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Update"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Update"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ScheduleBuilder":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A result builder that collects the systems written in a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"’s closure."}],"role":"symbol","title":"ScheduleBuilder","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduleBuilder","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedulebuilder","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScheduleBuilder"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScheduleBuilder"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ResourceWriter":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A system parameter that reads and writes a resource.","type":"text"}],"title":"ResourceWriter","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/resourcewriter","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceWriter","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ResourceWriter"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ResourceWriter"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ForwardEvents":{"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/forwardevents","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ForwardEvents","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ForwardEvents","kind":"symbol","title":"ForwardEvents","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ForwardEvents","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A system that yields each event of one type to an asynchronous stream, so code outside the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"schedule can await the events.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare the rules of a simulation as systems, and run them on a world in a schedule."}],"title":"Systems","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/systems"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A list of systems that run on a world, in order, and at the same time where they can.","type":"text"}],"title":"Schedule","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Schedule"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Schedule"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/UpdateEvents":{"abstract":[{"text":"A system that ends the current event update, dropping events old enough that every reader","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"has had its chance to read them.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UpdateEvents"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/UpdateEvents","title":"UpdateEvents","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/updateevents","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UpdateEvents"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule/ambiguities()":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns every pair of systems whose accesses conflict but that no ordering constraint"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"orders."}],"title":"ambiguities()","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule\/ambiguities()","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguities()","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ambiguities","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Ambiguity","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Systems9AmbiguityV"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemSet":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A type that names a group of systems, so ordering constraints can refer to all of them at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"once."}],"role":"symbol","title":"SystemSet","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemset","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SystemSet","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SystemSet","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/RemovedComponents":{"abstract":[{"text":"A system parameter that lists the entities that lost a component since the system last read","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"them.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"RemovedComponents","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/RemovedComponents","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/removedcomponents","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RemovedComponents","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RemovedComponents","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/EventWriter":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system parameter that sends events of one type."}],"role":"symbol","title":"EventWriter","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventWriter","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/eventwriter","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EventWriter"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EventWriter"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/MainActorSystem":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system that runs on the main actor, for work that touches main-actor state such as a user"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"interface."}],"role":"symbol","title":"MainActorSystem","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/MainActorSystem","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/mainactorsystem","type":"